Note: This is a modified version of the A* search algorithm, but without using a heuristic. Instead of the heuristic, it uses an arbitrary order for visiting neighboring cells. Because of this, this function has the same time complexity as BFS (O(|E|+|V|), where |E| is the number of edges and |V| is the number of vertices, in this case, cells and their connections), O(b^d), where b is the branching factor and d is the depth. However it has the advantage of concentrating its search in the goal region, where the target is more likely to be.

