This algorithm is a variant of the Floyd-Warshall algorithm, but instead of computing the shortest path distance between all pairs of nodes directly, it uses the priority queue (`heapq`) to select the node with the minimum distance to relax next, which reduces the time complexity to O(n^3 log n) that is achieved by the original Floyd-Warshall algorithm's repeated use of a priority queue to find the minimum distance.

